From be71cb93e77ec8148b018888816b7dd4142f4bb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:08:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban provenance: reads_local_store shares
 scoped_sources' routing; pin the unnamed-host replica premise

Follow-up to PR #2013 review nits (t_01a1d41a82ced7d9).

1. reads_local_store claimed "the same rule" as scoped_sources but over-approximated:
   an empty ref, a qualified ref with an empty sid, or a gw/profile/sid ref whose
   outer gateway/profile contradicts the scope was reported as a read, while
   scoped_sources answers those unknown without one (a map miss then failed closed:
   safe, but not the documented rule). Both now share one helper (_local_scope), and
   reads_local_store takes the profile scope; machine_verdicts and LinkVerdicts pass it.
   Test: for a mixed corpus x gateway x profile x local name, reads_local_store is
   true exactly when scoped_sources opens a home (RED at base: 12 cases).

2. LinkVerdicts.read leaves the replica unopened without a hub.db gateway name. Kept,
   with the premise now stated and tested: chat_gateway is NOT NULL in the synced
   schema (no bare replica link exists), and with no local name scoped_sources
   answers every named ref without a read, so a map miss gets the per-row verdict
   and no state.db read under write_txn. Opening the replica there would also break
   the all-local laziness test_all_local_backfill_never_opens_replica pins.
